  <ym-title|Assembly audit><label|assembly-audit>

  The chapter is explicitly conditional and assembles only the same-family
  interfaces actually stated in Chapters12\U18. It does not mark open
  quantitative inputs as proved. Groups1\U3 concern existence/reconstruction;
  group4 is needed for the trace asymptotic; group5 is needed for finite OPE.
  The conservative contact extension requires only polynomial separated
  bounds and common invariant degree decomposition.

  The final statement retains full ultraviolet limit first, then one common
  volume subsequence; auxiliary coefficient selections are not substituted
  for observable convergence. All phase statements refer to characters of the
  mixed compression algebra. No mass gap, phase uniqueness, simultaneous
  limit, phasewise lattice realization or contact positivity is asserted.

  Final cross-chapter review must update this chapter as specific analytic
  interfaces are discharged, without silently strengthening its scope.
